{
  "text": "G’day. Jonesy here, introducing you to Geoff’s Guide. Let’s work through the tabs, from left to right.\n\nForm gives you our original view of the race: the shortlist, the full field, and the form behind each runner. Start here to see who comes out on top.\n\nLate mail brings in what changes as the day unfolds: conditions, scratchings, riders and fresh information. See our revised selection beside the original, and understand what moved it.\n\nTips brings together leading racing tipsters. Explore the collective view, then open each tip to see the reasoning, the assumed conditions, and the run that horse needs.\n\nThe Ladder connects the form. If two horses have met, who beat whom, and by how much? If they haven’t, a shared opponent can help connect them. It’s another way to weigh the evidence, rather than a guaranteed finishing order.\n\nAnd Results shows how Geoff’s selections performed, alongside the jockeys, trainers and tipsters having a day out.\n\nCome back five minutes before the jump for the latest saved late mail and race preview—Geoff’s edge. Happy punting!",
